  "body": "### What are you trying to do\n\nI copied the shipped grblHAL machine in the Machines pane, changed it and saved it. The\nfile goes to the user machines folder (`%APPDATA%\\camcraft\\machines` on Windows).\n\nThe Setup page cannot find this machine:\n\n- The \"Library\" list shows only the shipped machines (`library_row` in\n  `crates/ui/src/egui_app/machine_page.rs`). When my machine is on the setup, it shows\n  \"other\".\n- \"Load other\" does not open in the user machines folder.\n\nNow only View > Machines > \"Use for this setup\" finds it.\n\n### How you imagine it working\n\n- The \"Library\" list shows the user machines first, then a separator, then the shipped\n  machines. A user who made a machine most likely wants to use it. The list reads the\n  same catalogue as the Machines pane (`library::enumerate`).\n- A user machine shows its name and file name.\n- A selection queues `UseCatalogueMachine(MachineSource::File(..))`, as \"Use for this\n  setup\" does. Undo puts the previous machine back.\n- A refused file shows \"[refused]\" and its reason, as in the Machines pane. It cannot be\n  selected.\n- \"Load other\" opens in the user machines folder when the folder exists.\n- The browser build has no such folder. There, nothing changes.\n\nTests: a UI test selects a machine from a temporary user folder, then undoes it. A test\nshows that a refused file cannot be selected.\n\nI want to do this work. I will claim the issue and open a draft PR.",
